TL;DR — Here’s a **Unity (2022/2023) OpenXR** vertical slice you can drop into a clean project and **build to Meta Quest 3**: procedurally spawns a small dungeon, VR locomotion (smooth + snap + dash “SPD”), destructible blocks, basic enemies, and Diablo-style loot rolls. No heavy packages required; runs with **OpenXR + InputDevices** (no XR Interaction Toolkit) for a fast start. Later, you can swap in XRIT and URP. Unity/OpenXR/URP + comfort options are chosen per your design brief for Quest 3. fileciteturn0file1 fileciteturn0file0

# Plan (pseudocode)

1) **Bootstrap (Editor/runtime)**
   - Ensure Android target (ARM64), Linear color space, Vulkan/GLES3.
   - Create/start a sample scene at runtime if none exists.
   - Create “PlayerRig” with CharacterController + HMD camera (TrackedPoseDriver).

2) **Locomotion (“SPD”)**
   - Read controller thumbsticks via `UnityEngine.XR.InputDevices`.
   - Left stick: smooth move; right stick: snap turn; A/X: short dash/teleport-like blink.
   - Optional comfort vignette during fast motion.

3) **Procedural Dungeon**
   - Generate N modular rooms connected by corridors.
   - Build rooms from large blocks (1m) that can be destroyed.

4) **Destruction**
   - Ray from camera (or right controller forward) on button press hits `DestructibleBlock`.
   - Replace with pooled debris pieces; auto-settle and clean up.

5) **Enemies + Combat**
   - Simple seekers that approach player; basic HP.
   - Player ray “spell” damages enemies; on death spawn loot.

6) **Loot System**
   - Item rarity tiers + affix rolls; spawn physical pickup with short physics burst.
   - Show picked item summary in a worldspace canvas.

7) **Director (tiny seed)**
   - Track time since last combat + player HP proxy; spawn help or heat up waves.

8) **Build**
   - Switch to Android, set OpenXR in Project Settings (one-time).
   - Press Play (PCVR) or Build & Run (Quest 3).

> Why these choices: Unity + URP/OpenXR is the recommended Quest-3 path, modular dungeon + destructible chunks match the design doc; SPD locomotion options + snap turn/teleport align with comfort guidance. fileciteturn0file1

